WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
OK.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:08.900
Let's start today with a story about the failings
of most Democrats in the United States, elected

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.480
Democrats now.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.000
I'm still on the left.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.790
The Democratic Party is a center left party.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.030
I'm a progressive.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.360
This is a left wing channel.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.530
We criticize the right all the time today.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.980
I'm going to criticize Democrats on their
response to the police protest.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.800
So let me set the stage for you.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.900
Republicans, of course, have completely and
utterly failed in their response to the protests,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.770
with the exception of, for example, like Republican
Senator Mitt Romney, who showed up and marched

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:40.359
with protesters and said Black Lives Matter,
which was mostly mostly just a political show,

00:00:40.359 --> 00:00:44.750
although I think it's an important action
and an important political show, but it's

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.999
essentially a political show.

00:00:46.999 --> 00:00:51.730
Republicans have refused to admit that there
are systemic problems that need to be dealt

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:52.730
with.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:55.489
Kaley McEnany did this yesterday during her
press briefing.

00:00:55.489 --> 00:01:02.329
Instead, they focus on phrases like sometimes
there will be instances of racism or bad apples.

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:09.369
But meanwhile, they often support using even
more force against protesters who are protesting

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.670
against police brutality.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.880
So the right is off the deep end.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:20.119
I've also criticized some of the activists
on the left who I believe are taking the wrong

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:24.119
approach, for example, with defund or abolish
the police.

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:29.009
I already explained yesterday in detail why
I think that's the wrong approach.

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:36.659
But today, the point is I want to focus on
the failure, the abject failure of the Democratic

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:38.399
Party leadership itself.

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:43.409
This was a beautiful opportunity for the Democratic
Party to dramatically distinguish itself from

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:44.649
the Republican Party.

00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:48.820
I often talk about on many issues, Democrats
and Republicans are very different.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.050
Sometimes they're very similar.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:55.650
Here was an opportunity for Democrats to put
together a blistering systemic critique of

00:01:55.650 --> 00:02:01.619
how we got to where we are with the protests
as an outlet for much of what is going wrong

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:02.619
in our country.

00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:09.729
If you listen or watch, listen to or watch
the clip from last Monday's show, I broke

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.640
down how this is not just about police brutality.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.890
You need to look at this more systemically.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.290
What we're seeing is not just about racism.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.860
It's not just about capitalism.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:25.020
It's not just about health care or culture.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.290
It's all of these things together.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:32.990
And you need a wide ranging systemic critique
to appreciate everything that has gotten us

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.580
to where we are today.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:39.220
And bias in policing is a big part of that,
Democrats overall.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:45.280
And by this, I mean elected Democrats, particularly
House leadership and Democrats in the Senate

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.320
first really did nothing.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:52.590
Eventually, they said, yeah, we support protests
against police brutality.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:58.980
They participated in a bunch of photo ops,
which mean meaningful in a sense, but doesn't

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:02.770
really create a systemic critique of what's
going on.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:06.690
And it's great that Nancy Pelosi joined protesters
and talked to people.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:09.510
It's important that Elizabeth Warren joined
a protest.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:14.920
It's great that Democratic presidential candidate
Joe Biden went and spoke to protesters.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:22.590
But this would have been a perfect opportunity
for a big systemic critique that combines

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.800
everything from our economic system.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.290
Problem with wages, wealth inequality, are
voting system.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.050
So many other components.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.960
This was the opportunity to change the narrative
or create a narrative.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:39.810
It could have been like the Occupy Wall Street
moment where income inequality and wealth

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.740
inequality went mainstream.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.560
You had Republicans and Democrats disagreeing
about what should be done about it.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.750
But Occupy Wall Street mainstreamed the topic
of wealth and income inequality.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:56.810
Instead, what we got from most Democrats is
this mild support of protesters, cautious,

00:03:56.810 --> 00:04:01.470
of course, never to support the tactics that
were used and very quick to focus on how they

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.060
don't agree with many of the tactics, which
is fine.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:10.610
But they're missing the real big opportunity
in conjunction with some totally farcical,

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:15.040
performative events like the video that we're
showing our radio or our video audience right

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:20.239
now of House and Senate Democrats kneeling
for eight minutes and 46 seconds in honor

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:21.239
of George Floyd.

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:23.920
It is totally performative.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:29.190
I'd be fine with it if it came with a big
systemic critique.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:35.570
And we've been sounding the alarm for years
about that sort of necessary systemic critique

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:39.200
because there are so many different systems
that need to change now.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:47.360
In addition to Democrats not leaving a valid
systemic criticism in terms of the systems

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:50.620
that got us where we are and need to be changed.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:57.420
There also haven't been any real big comments
from establishment Democrats about the civil

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:59.380
liberties totalitarianism.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:05.380
Argument Republicans have been going hard,
demanding the military come in, tougher policing,

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:06.760
all of this stuff.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:11.450
And Democrats have sort of meekly opposed
the tactics, said we were not in in agreement

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:17.740
with the military coming in, but they've not
really gone after, hey, not only is sending

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.800
the military in wrong.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:26.710
But Republicans have spent years criminalizing
civil disobedience, criminalizing poverty,

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:32.520
criminalizing journalism, much like with the
ag gag laws, which now can be tied into the

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:37.690
protests as we see some journalists just straight
up beaten, hit with shields and batons and

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.690
nightsticks.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:43.490
There is a much bigger story here that the
country is primed for right now, which Democrats

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:44.710
could be taking advantage of.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:52.670
And they have not talking about how so much
about protesters rights is inextricably linked

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:59.520
to our surveillance state, warrantless wiretapping,
NSA surveillance, sting ray devices.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:07.270
My point here is that there is so much that
is bigger than we like the protesters and

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:11.410
Trump shouldn't send in the military and police
brutality is bad.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.510
Now, why aren't Democrats doing it?

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.350
There's a couple of perspectives.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:19.530
One explanation would be Democrats aren't
doing it because the Democratic Party is very

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:22.030
centrist and they don't really believe in
all that stuff.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.250
That's true.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:28.460
But to some degree, definitely it is not true
about all Democrats.

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:35.060
There are many Democrats who are keeping quiet
for political expediency, for a calculation

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:41.570
that it's better for their reelection if they
don't talk about that stuff in this context.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:44.410
Maybe they're making the right calculation
for their reelection.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:45.750
Maybe they're not.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:48.130
But this is a huge missed opportunity.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:54.330
And this is one of the areas where the scope
of debate has been narrowed dramatically,

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:58.550
where there should be a big systemic critique
from Democrats here.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:02.250
And instead, we are getting the military shouldn't
come in.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.160
Police brutality is a problem.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:08.810
And missing so much of what could really change
the dialog in this country.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:13.690
This is a failure, a moral failure by Democrats,
whether it's a strategic failure.

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:14.690
Maybe it's not.

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:18.980
I mean, maybe maybe they're making the right
strategic calculation in terms of their reelections.

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:19.551
But the moral failure is impossible to ignore.

